  "live_records": {
    "q-350600": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350600",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the sum of the following series. Do not round the answer.\n\n$1-\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{4}{49}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{2}^{n}}{{7}^{n}}+⋯=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing we notice is that we can rewrite the terms of the series as powers of $\\frac{2}{7}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{4}{49}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{2}^{n}}{{7}^{n}}+⋯ & =1-\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{{2}^{2}}{{7}^{2}}+⋯+(-1)^{n}\\frac{{2}^{n}}{{7}^{n}}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{7}+{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{2}+⋯+(-1)^{n}{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{n}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1+x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1+x} & =1-x+{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+⋯+(-1)^{n}{x}^{n}+⋯\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{2}{7}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1+\\frac{2}{7})} & =1-\\frac{2}{7}+{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{2}-{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{3}+⋯+(-1)^{n}{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{n}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{7}{9} & =1-\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{4}{49}-\\frac{8}{343}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{2}^{n}}{{7}^{n}}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\frac{7}{9}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
